= ZHANG, Qi -- Teaching
[https://feg.um.edu.mo/cee/ Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering], [https://www.um.edu.mo/ University of Macau]

== Current classes
- /[https://feg.um.edu.mo/cee/courses/msccourses_from2023/ CIVL7014: Numerical Modeling in Geomechanics]/ (PG).
- /[https://feg.um.edu.mo/cee/courses/msccoursescpm_from2024/ CIVL7208: Special Topics in Construction Project Management]/ (PG).
- /CIVL7998\/CIVL7298: Project Report/ (PG).
- /[https://feg.um.edu.mo/cee/courses/bsccourses_from2021/ CIVL4011: Application of Numerical Methods in Geotechnical Engineering]/ (UG).

== Courses I have contributed to
- /CIVL8002: Frontiers of Modern Civil Engineering/ ([https://www.um.edu.mo/ University of Macau]). I taught the sections on regression and regularization (Ridge and LASSO).
- /CSE583: Analytical and Numerical Methods in Geotechnical Engineering/ ([https://www.polyu.edu.hk/ The Hong Kong Polytechnic University]). I taught the sections on soil constitutive modeling, limit equilibrium and limit analysis, and slope stability analysis.
- /CE620: Research Methods/ ([https://www.polyu.edu.hk/ The Hong Kong Polytechnic University]). I taught the sections on probability and hypothesis testing.
- /CEE314: Computational Poromechanics/ ([https://www.stanford.edu/ Stanford University]). I led two ABAQUS tutorial sessions.
